<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Manual TalkGroup number entry:<br><br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#manual-talkgroup-number-entry" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... mber-entry</a><br><br>N1KY</div></blockquote>Craig: what a terrific feature; thank you!<br><br>Makes OpenGD77 worth the price of admission.  I am now freed to watch and listen to the Hoseline and jump into conversations on an ad hoc basis!<br><br>I seem to be timing out and I did read about TOT in the Guide.  I found the Sound Option of Timeout Beep of 10s, but I am getting no sound alert and how to I set my TOT for a greater amount of time?  Thank you in advance.</div></blockquote>TOT is set on a per channel basis, and can be done in the CPS or the firmware (Channel Details screen).<br><br>If not TOT is set, i.e is set to 0; the timer counts upwards showing how long you have been transmitting<br><br>If TOT is set to a value other than 0 then the timer counts down.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Mar 17, 2024 2:28 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
